<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Theoretical Proofs</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Standing assumptions.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We make the following assumptions throughout the appendix (stated explicitly here to keep proofs self-contained):</p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A1)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Consistent ordering.</span> The ordering constraint set <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{order}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>order</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{order}}</annotation></semantics></math> is acyclic (i.e., contains no contradictory pairs).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A2)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Convexified normalization.</span> For theoretical statements we replace the RMS equality by the convex ball constraint <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}\leq N</annotation></semantics></math> (practical solvers may enforce equality or use penalties; see discussion in the main text). This yields a closed, convex and bounded feasible set when combined with linear constraints.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A3)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bounded policy gradients and smoothness.</span> The policy is such that <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p,a}\|\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p)\|^{2}\leq G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p,a}\|\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p)\|^{2}\leq G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1 (Unbiasedness []). ‣ Key assumptions. ‣ 3.5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>: Unbiasedness of Gradient Estimate</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Unbiasedness of Gradient Estimate <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wil92</a>]</cite>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid p)</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(p)</annotation></semantics></math> be any deterministic function of the prefix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}=(r-\alpha V(p))\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}=(r-\alpha V(p))\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p,a}[\widehat{g}]=\nabla J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p,a}[\widehat{g}]=\nabla J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the policy gradient theorem with a state-dependent baseline <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(p)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla J(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{p,a}\big[(r-b(p))\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p)\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla J(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{p,a}\big[(r-b(p))\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(p)=\alpha V(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(p)=\alpha V(p)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p,a}[\alpha V(p)\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p)]=\mathbb{E}_{p}\!\Big[\alpha V(p)\,\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid p)}[\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p)]\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p,a}[\alpha V(p)\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p)]=\mathbb{E}_{p}\!\Big[\alpha V(p)\,\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid p)}[\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p)]\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">But <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi}[\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p)]=\nabla_{\theta}\sum_{a}\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p)=\nabla_{\theta}1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi}[\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p)]=\nabla_{\theta}\sum_{a}\pi_{\theta}(a\mid p)=\nabla_{\theta}1=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so the baseline term vanishes. Hence <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\widehat{g}]=\nabla J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\widehat{g}]=\nabla J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 3.2 (Optimality of Expectation Baseline []). ‣ Comment. ‣ 3.5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>: Optimality of Expectation Baseline</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Expectation Minimizes Variance<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx7" title="" class="ltx_ref">GBB04</a>]</cite>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Among all deterministic functions <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(p)</annotation></semantics></math>, the choice <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(p)=\mathbb{E}[r\mid p]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(p)=\mathbb{E}[r\mid p]</annotation></semantics></math> (and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math>) minimizes <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[r-\alpha V(p)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[r-\alpha V(p)]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the law of total variance for <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=r-\alpha V(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=r-\alpha V(p)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[A]=\mathbb{E}_{p}[\operatorname{Var}[A\mid p]]+\operatorname{Var}_{p}[\mathbb{E}[A\mid p]]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[A]=\mathbb{E}_{p}[\operatorname{Var}[A\mid p]]+\operatorname{Var}_{p}[\mathbb{E}[A\mid p]].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(p)</annotation></semantics></math> is deterministic given <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[A\mid p]=\operatorname{Var}[r\mid p]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[A\mid p]=\operatorname{Var}[r\mid p]</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[A\mid p]=\mathbb{E}[r\mid p]-\alpha V(p)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[A\mid p]=\mathbb{E}[r\mid p]-\alpha V(p).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[A]=\mathbb{E}_{p}[\operatorname{Var}[r\mid p]]+\operatorname{Var}_{p}[\mathbb{E}[r\mid p]-\alpha V(p)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[A]=\mathbb{E}_{p}[\operatorname{Var}[r\mid p]]+\operatorname{Var}_{p}[\mathbb{E}[r\mid p]-\alpha V(p)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">The first term is fixed; the second is minimized by setting <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha V(p)=\mathbb{E}[r\mid p]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha V(p)=\mathbb{E}[r\mid p]</annotation></semantics></math>, which yields the stated result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3 (Tree-Induced Advantage Structure and Inductive Bias). ‣ Comment. ‣ 3.5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>: Tree-Induced Advantage Structure</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now formalize the SAE projection used in the main text in a convex form suitable for theoretical guarantees.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Tree-Induced Advantage Structure)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be the observed rewards in a group and let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{order}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>order</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{order}}</annotation></semantics></math> be an acyclic set of pairwise ordering relations. Consider the convex QP</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.Ex23X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{a}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{a}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\arg\min_{\bm{a}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}}\ \|\bm{a}-\bm{r}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒓</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\arg\min_{\bm{a}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}}\ \|\bm{a}-\bm{r}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 3.2 Staged Advantage Estimation as Constrained Quadratic Program ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>–convex)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.Ex23Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{s.t.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">s.t.</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{s.t.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{1}^{\top}\bm{a}=0,\qquad\|\bm{a}\|^{2}\leq N," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{1}^{\top}\bm{a}=0,\qquad\|\bm{a}\|^{2}\leq N,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.Ex23Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{i}+\delta_{ij}\leq a_{j}\quad\forall(i,j)\in\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{order}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>order</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{i}+\delta_{ij}\leq a_{j}\quad\forall(i,j)\in\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{order}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with fixed margin <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{ij}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{ij}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Under Assumption (A​1) the feasible set is nonempty and convex, the objective is strictly convex, and the problem has a unique solution <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies all linear ordering constraints, so that for each <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\in\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{order}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>order</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\in\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{order}}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{*}+\delta\leq a_{j}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{*}+\delta\leq a_{j}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">With linear equalities/inequalities and the convex ball <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{a}\|^{2}\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{a}\|^{2}\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>, the feasible set is convex and closed. The objective <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{a}-\bm{r}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒓</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{a}-\bm{r}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly convex (Hessian <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2I\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2I\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>). A strictly convex function on a nonempty convex compact set has a unique minimizer, so <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> exists and is unique. The ordering constraints are explicit linear constraints in the program, hence the minimizer satisfies them by construction.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Practical remark.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In practice we solve a softened variant (penalty or SLSQP with equality RMS); Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Experimental Setup: Hyperparameters and Model Configuration ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> discusses numerical choices. The convex formulation above is used only for the theoretical guarantees (existence, uniqueness, and structural encoding).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 (Tree Constraints Improve Gradient Signal). ‣ Comment. ‣ 3.5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>: Gradient Signal Improvement</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Gradient Signal and Structure)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under assumptions (A1)–(A3), let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be observed rewards in a group. Define the centered reward vector</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}_{0}\;=\;\bm{r}-\overline{\bm{r}}\,\mathbf{1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒓</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒓</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}_{0}\;=\;\bm{r}-\overline{\bm{r}}\,\mathbf{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and let</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{0}\;=\;\{\,\bm{a}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}:\;\mathbf{1}^{\top}\bm{a}=0,\;\|\bm{a}\|^{2}\leq N,\;L\bm{a}\leq\mathbf{0}\,\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{0}\;=\;\{\,\bm{a}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}:\;\mathbf{1}^{\top}\bm{a}=0,\;\|\bm{a}\|^{2}\leq N,\;L\bm{a}\leq\mathbf{0}\,\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the rows of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}^{\top}-e_{j}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}^{\top}-e_{j}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\in\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{order}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>order</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\in\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{order}}</annotation></semantics></math> (zero-margin pairwise orderings). Assume <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0}\in\mathcal{F}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0}\in\mathcal{F}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (holds under zero margins and acyclicity). Let</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{*}\;=\;\arg\min_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{F}_{0}}\|\bm{a}-\bm{r}_{0}\|^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{*}\;=\;\arg\min_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{F}_{0}}\|\bm{a}-\bm{r}_{0}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">be the Euclidean projection of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Variance non-increase) </span><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}]\leq\operatorname{Var}[\bm{r}_{0}]=\operatorname{Var}[\bm{r}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝒓</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}]\leq\operatorname{Var}[\bm{r}_{0}]=\operatorname{Var}[\bm{r}].</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Gradient variance bound) If samples are i.i.d. and (A3) holds, the Monte–Carlo gradient estimator with mean-centered advantages satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}\!\Bigg(\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}a_{k}^{*}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\hat{c}_{k}\mid p_{k})\Bigg)\leq\frac{1}{K}\,G^{2}\,\operatorname{Var}[a^{*}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}\!\Bigg(\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}a_{k}^{*}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\hat{c}_{k}\mid p_{k})\Bigg)\leq\frac{1}{K}\,G^{2}\,\operatorname{Var}[a^{*}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, equality in (1) holds iff <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}_{0}\in\mathcal{F}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}_{0}\in\mathcal{F}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise the inequality is strict.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove the two claims in order.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(1) Variance non-increase via convex projection.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By construction <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Euclidean projection of <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> onto the closed convex set <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Projection optimality (firm nonexpansiveness / characterization of the projector; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx2" title="" class="ltx_ref">BC17</a>, Thm. 3.14]</cite>) gives the variational inequality</p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\bm{r}_{0}-\bm{a}^{*},\,\bm{z}-\bm{a}^{*}\rangle\leq 0\qquad\forall\bm{z}\in\mathcal{F}_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\bm{r}_{0}-\bm{a}^{*},\,\bm{z}-\bm{a}^{*}\rangle\leq 0\qquad\forall\bm{z}\in\mathcal{F}_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0}\in\mathcal{F}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0}\in\mathcal{F}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> we may take <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding</p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\bm{r}_{0}-\bm{a}^{*},\ -\bm{a}^{*}\rangle\leq 0\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\langle\bm{r}_{0}-\bm{a}^{*},\ \bm{a}^{*}\rangle\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\bm{r}_{0}-\bm{a}^{*},\ -\bm{a}^{*}\rangle\leq 0\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\langle\bm{r}_{0}-\bm{a}^{*},\ \bm{a}^{*}\rangle\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{a}^{*}\|^{2}\leq\langle\bm{r}_{0},\bm{a}^{*}\rangle\leq\|\bm{r}_{0}\|\,\|\bm{a}^{*}\|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{a}^{*}\|^{2}\leq\langle\bm{r}_{0},\bm{a}^{*}\rangle\leq\|\bm{r}_{0}\|\,\|\bm{a}^{*}\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and dividing by <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{a}^{*}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{a}^{*}\|</annotation></semantics></math> (if <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{*}\neq\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{*}\neq\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>) gives <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{a}^{*}\|\leq\|\bm{r}_{0}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{a}^{*}\|\leq\|\bm{r}_{0}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{*}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{*}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> the inequality is trivial. Because both <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> are zero-mean, their population variances satisfy</p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}]\;=\;\frac{1}{N}\|\bm{a}^{*}\|^{2}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{N}\|\bm{r}_{0}\|^{2}\;=\;\operatorname{Var}[\bm{r}_{0}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}]\;=\;\frac{1}{N}\|\bm{a}^{*}\|^{2}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{N}\|\bm{r}_{0}\|^{2}\;=\;\operatorname{Var}[\bm{r}_{0}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">which proves (1).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The inequality is strict exactly when <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}_{0}\notin\mathcal{F}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}_{0}\notin\mathcal{F}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (otherwise the projection returns <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and norms are equal). Thus whenever the centered rewards violate at least one tree constraint the projection strictly reduces squared norm (hence variance).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Role of the ordering constraints.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The linear order constraints <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\bm{a}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\bm{a}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> encode <em id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">tree consistency</em> by enforcing prefix-relative advantage orderings.
With the convexified normalization <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{a}\|^{2}\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{a}\|^{2}\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>, the feasible set</p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{0}=\bigl\{\bm{a}:\mathbf{1}^{\top}\bm{a}=0,\;\;\|\bm{a}\|^{2}\leq N,\;\;L\bm{a}\leq 0\bigr\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.449em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{0}=\bigl\{\bm{a}:\mathbf{1}^{\top}\bm{a}=0,\;\;\|\bm{a}\|^{2}\leq N,\;\;L\bm{a}\leq 0\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is closed, convex, and contains <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟎</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the Euclidean projection</p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{*}=\mathrm{Proj}_{\mathcal{F}_{0}}(\bm{r}_{0})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{*}=\mathrm{Proj}_{\mathcal{F}_{0}}(\bm{r}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">satisfies <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{a}^{*}\|\leq\|\bm{r}_{0}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{a}^{*}\|\leq\|\bm{r}_{0}\|</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}]\leq\operatorname{Var}[\bm{r}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝒓</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}]\leq\operatorname{Var}[\bm{r}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">If the unconstrained (GRPO) projection already respects the orderings, the two projections coincide. Otherwise, <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> enforces the tree structure by making the minimal modification (in Euclidean norm) to <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> necessary to satisfy the order constraints. In practice, this structural correction typically—and often strictly—reduces the advantage variance across prefixes when <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> violates tree constraints.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Note, however, that there is no universal monotonicity guarantee comparing
<math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{Proj}_{\mathcal{F}_{0}}(\bm{r}_{0})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{Proj}_{\mathcal{F}_{0}}(\bm{r}_{0})\|</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{Proj}_{H}(\bm{r}_{0})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Proj</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{Proj}_{H}(\bm{r}_{0})\|</annotation></semantics></math> for every possible <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (projections onto nested convex sets need not be ordered). Consequently, we present the projection variance bound as the rigorous core result and treat the additional empirical benefit relative to plain GRPO as an expected, often-observed effect supported by experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(2) Gradient variance bound.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=a^{*}(p)\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\hat{c}\mid p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=a^{*}(p)\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\hat{c}\mid p)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the single-sample gradient random vector. For the minibatch estimator <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{G}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}g_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{G}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}g_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with i.i.d. <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[\widehat{G}]=\frac{1}{K}\operatorname{Var}[g]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[\widehat{G}]=\frac{1}{K}\operatorname{Var}[g].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Compute</p>
<table id="A1.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[g]=\mathbb{E}\|g\|^{2}-\|\mathbb{E}[g]\|^{2}\leq\mathbb{E}\|g\|^{2}=\mathbb{E}\big[(a^{*})^{2}\|\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\|^{2}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[g]=\mathbb{E}\|g\|^{2}-\|\mathbb{E}[g]\|^{2}\leq\mathbb{E}\|g\|^{2}=\mathbb{E}\big[(a^{*})^{2}\|\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\|^{2}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Using the uniform second-moment bound on the score from (A3) (i.e. <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\|^{2}\leq G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\|^{2}\leq G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) and mean-centering of <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get the conservative bound</p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[g]\leq G^{2}\,\mathbb{E}[(a^{*})^{2}]=G^{2}\,\operatorname{Var}[a^{*}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[g]\leq G^{2}\,\mathbb{E}[(a^{*})^{2}]=G^{2}\,\operatorname{Var}[a^{*}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Therefore</p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[\widehat{G}]\leq\frac{1}{K}\,G^{2}\,\operatorname{Var}[a^{*}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[\widehat{G}]\leq\frac{1}{K}\,G^{2}\,\operatorname{Var}[a^{*}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">which proves claim (2).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>GRPO as a Degenerate Projection and Variance Comparison</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.5</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(SAE does not increase variance; strict reduction under violations)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be observed rewards and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{0}=\mathbf{r}-\bar{r}\mathbf{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{0}=\mathbf{r}-\bar{r}\mathbf{1}</annotation></semantics></math> the centered rewards.
Assume <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}\subseteq H:=\{\mathbf{a}:\mathbf{1}^{\top}\mathbf{a}=0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐚</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}\subseteq H:=\{\mathbf{a}:\mathbf{1}^{\top}\mathbf{a}=0\}</annotation></semantics></math> is closed, convex and satisfies <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0}\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0}\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}\leq N</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}^{*}=\Pi_{\mathcal{F}}(\mathbf{r}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}^{*}=\Pi_{\mathcal{F}}(\mathbf{r}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> (SAE projection) and
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}=\mathbf{r}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>GRPO</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}=\mathbf{r}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (plain mean-centering).
If <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{0}\neq\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{0}\neq\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> define the std-normalized GRPO vector
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO\_std}}=\sqrt{N}\,\mathbf{r}_{0}/\|\mathbf{r}_{0}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mi>GRPO</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>std</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO\_std}}=\sqrt{N}\,\mathbf{r}_{0}/\|\mathbf{r}_{0}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}^{*}]\leq\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{r}_{0}]=\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>GRPO</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}^{*}]\leq\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{r}_{0}]=\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, with strict inequality whenever </span><math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{0}\notin\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{0}\notin\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the nondegenerate case </span><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{0}\neq\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{0}\neq\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}^{*}]\leq 1=\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO\_std}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mi>GRPO</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>std</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}^{*}]\leq 1=\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO\_std}}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">; hence SAE never increases variance relative to GRPO with std-normalization.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, when centered rewards violate tree-order constraints the SAE projection typically (and often strictly) reduces variance compared to plain mean-centering.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">(1) By definition <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Euclidean projection of <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> onto the closed convex set <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. Projection optimality yields, for all <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{r}_{0}-\mathbf{a}^{*},\ \mathbf{z}-\mathbf{a}^{*}\rangle\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{r}_{0}-\mathbf{a}^{*},\ \mathbf{z}-\mathbf{a}^{*}\rangle\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}=\mathbf{0}\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}=\mathbf{0}\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{r}_{0}-\mathbf{a}^{*},\ \mathbf{a}^{*}\rangle\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{r}_{0}-\mathbf{a}^{*},\ \mathbf{a}^{*}\rangle\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Expanding norms:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{r}_{0}\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{r}_{0}-\mathbf{a}^{*}\|^{2}+2\langle\mathbf{r}_{0}-\mathbf{a}^{*},\mathbf{a}^{*}\rangle+\|\mathbf{a}^{*}\|^{2}\geq\|\mathbf{a}^{*}\|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{r}_{0}\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{r}_{0}-\mathbf{a}^{*}\|^{2}+2\langle\mathbf{r}_{0}-\mathbf{a}^{*},\mathbf{a}^{*}\rangle+\|\mathbf{a}^{*}\|^{2}\geq\|\mathbf{a}^{*}\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">hence <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{a}^{*}\|^{2}\leq\|\mathbf{r}_{0}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{a}^{*}\|^{2}\leq\|\mathbf{r}_{0}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Dividing by <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}^{*}]\leq\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{r}_{0}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}^{*}]\leq\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{r}_{0}]</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{0}\notin\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{0}\notin\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{r}_{0}-\mathbf{a}^{*}\|&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{r}_{0}-\mathbf{a}^{*}\|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and the inequality is strict.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">(2) For <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{0}\neq\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{0}\neq\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> the std-normalized GRPO vector has <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO\_std}}\|^{2}=N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mi>GRPO</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>std</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO\_std}}\|^{2}=N</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO\_std}}]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mi>GRPO</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>std</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO\_std}}]=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Since by assumption every <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{a}^{*}\|^{2}\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{a}^{*}\|^{2}\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}^{*}]\leq 1=\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO\_std}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mi>GRPO</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>std</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}^{*}]\leq 1=\operatorname{Var}[\mathbf{a}_{\mathrm{GRPO\_std}}]</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves that SAE does not increase variance compared to GRPO with std-normalization.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 3.5 (Sample Efficiency via Variance Reduction). ‣ Comment. ‣ 3.5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>: Sample Complexity via Variance Reduction</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.6</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Sample Efficiency and Convergence Rate)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the objective <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth. From Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 (Tree Constraints Improve Gradient Signal). ‣ Comment. ‣ 3.5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, the variance of the policy gradient estimator using SAE advantages <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}\leq G^{2}\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}\leq G^{2}\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the bound on the squared norm of the log-policy gradients. Under these conditions, the number of iterations <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> required for Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD) to find an <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary point (i.e., <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta)\|^{2}\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta)\|^{2}\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>) is given by:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=O\left(\frac{LG^{2}\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}]}{\epsilon}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=O\left(\frac{LG^{2}\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}]}{\epsilon}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This directly links the variance of the SAE advantages to the sample efficiency of the optimization.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The standard convergence result for nonconvex SGD states that to reach an <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-stationary point, the required number of iterations <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> scales as <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=O(L\sigma^{2}/\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=O(L\sigma^{2}/\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx8" title="" class="ltx_ref">GL13</a>]</cite>. From Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 (Tree Constraints Improve Gradient Signal). ‣ Comment. ‣ 3.5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, we have a specific bound on the gradient variance for our estimator:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}\leq G^{2}\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}\leq G^{2}\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting our specific variance bound into the general complexity result directly yields:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=O\left(\frac{L(G^{2}\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}])}{\epsilon}\right)=O\left(\frac{LG^{2}\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}]}{\epsilon}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=O\left(\frac{L(G^{2}\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}])}{\epsilon}\right)=O\left(\frac{LG^{2}\operatorname{Var}[\bm{a}^{*}]}{\epsilon}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">This shows that the sample complexity is directly proportional to the variance of the SAE advantages.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>SAE Improves Estimation of the Best Consistent Value Function</h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall from Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 3.2 (Optimality of Expectation Baseline []). ‣ Comment. ‣ 3.5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> that the variance-minimizing deterministic baseline for a prefix is the true prefix-value</p>
<table id="A1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi}(p)\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi}\bigl[r(\tau)\mid\tau\supset p\bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊃</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi}(p)\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi}\bigl[r(\tau)\mid\tau\supset p\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">i.e. the expected terminal reward of trajectories that extend prefix <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We consider three concrete empirical/algorithmic estimators of <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{(GRPO, global)}\qquad V_{\mathrm{GRPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">(GRPO, global)</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>GRPO</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{(GRPO, global)}\qquad V_{\mathrm{GRPO}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;=\;\bar{r}\;=\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}r(\tau_{i})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;=\;\bar{r}\;=\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}r(\tau_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{(Subtree empirical / $V_{E}$)}\qquad V_{E}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">(Subtree empirical / </mtext><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">)</mtext></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{(Subtree empirical / $V_{E}$)}\qquad V_{E}(p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\;=\;\frac{1}{N_{p}^{\mathrm{sub}}}\sum_{\tau_{i}:\tau_{i}\supset p}r(\tau_{i})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>sub</mi></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊃</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;=\;\frac{1}{N_{p}^{\mathrm{sub}}}\sum_{\tau_{i}:\tau_{i}\supset p}r(\tau_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{(SAE / projected)}\qquad\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{SAE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">(SAE / projected)</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>SAE</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{(SAE / projected)}\qquad\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{SAE}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;=\;P_{\mathcal{C}}\!\bigl(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}\bigr),\qquad\widehat{V}_{\mathrm{SAE}}(p)\;=\;\bigl(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{SAE}}\bigr)_{p}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>GRPO</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>SAE</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>SAE</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;=\;P_{\mathcal{C}}\!\bigl(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}\bigr),\qquad\widehat{V}_{\mathrm{SAE}}(p)\;=\;\bigl(\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{SAE}}\bigr)_{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A1.SS7.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tau_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tau_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> are the sampled completions, <math id="A1.SS7.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p}^{\mathrm{sub}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>sub</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p}^{\mathrm{sub}}</annotation></semantics></math> counts all sampled completions that extend prefix <math id="A1.SS7.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS7.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>GRPO</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is the vector of per-prefix empirical exact-start means
<math id="A1.SS7.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}(p)=\tfrac{1}{n_{p}^{\mathrm{exact}}}\sum_{i:s_{i}=p}r(\tau_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>GRPO</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>exact</mi></msubsup></mfrac><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}(p)=\tfrac{1}{n_{p}^{\mathrm{exact}}}\sum_{i:s_{i}=p}r(\tau_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> (used as the input to projection).
The set <math id="A1.SS7.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\subset\mathbb{R}^{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\subset\mathbb{R}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the closed convex class of prefix-value vectors satisfying the tree-ordering constraints (convexified as needed).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Equation (<a href="#A1.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ A.7 SAE Improves Estimation of the Best Consistent Value Function ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Proofs ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) is the <em id="A1.SS7.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">idealized</em> prefix-space SAE: it projects the empirical per-prefix vector onto <math id="A1.SS7.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice we realize SAE by a sample-space projection (solve the QP in sample-space for advantages, then aggregate), which is equivalent to the prefix-space projection under Assumption A4 (constraints act only on prefix-aggregates); otherwise the two may differ slightly due to solver/regularization details.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.7</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(SAE optimally reduces estimation-to-class error)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{*}_{\mathcal{C}}=P_{\mathcal{C}}(\mathbf{V}^{\pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{*}_{\mathcal{C}}=P_{\mathcal{C}}(\mathbf{V}^{\pi})</annotation></semantics></math> be the projection of the true prefix-value vector onto <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any empirical GRPO prefix-vector <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>GRPO</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\|\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{SAE}}-\mathbf{V}^{*}_{\mathcal{C}}\big\|_{2}\;\leq\;\big\|\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}-\mathbf{V}^{*}_{\mathcal{C}}\big\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>SAE</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>GRPO</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\|\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{SAE}}-\mathbf{V}^{*}_{\mathcal{C}}\big\|_{2}\;\leq\;\big\|\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}-\mathbf{V}^{*}_{\mathcal{C}}\big\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with strict inequality whenever <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}\notin\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>GRPO</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}\notin\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Sketch.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS7.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Immediate from the distance-decreasing property of Euclidean projection onto a closed convex set: for every <math id="A1.SS7.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A1.SS7.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.SS7.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|P_{\mathcal{C}}(x)-z\|_{2}\leq\|x-z\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|P_{\mathcal{C}}(x)-z\|_{2}\leq\|x-z\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Set <math id="A1.SS7.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>GRPO</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\widehat{\mathbf{V}}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS7.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\mathbf{V}^{*}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\mathbf{V}^{*}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Comparison and limitations.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{E}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> vs <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{GRPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>GRPO</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{GRPO}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> The subtree estimator <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{E}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{E}(p)</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#A1.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ A.7 SAE Improves Estimation of the Best Consistent Value Function ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Proofs ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) trades variance for potential bias at each prefix. The MSE of an estimator is decomposed into its squared bias and variance: <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MSE}(\widehat{V})=\mathrm{Bias}(\widehat{V})^{2}+\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>MSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Bias</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MSE}(\widehat{V})=\mathrm{Bias}(\widehat{V})^{2}+\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{V})</annotation></semantics></math>. While <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{GRPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>GRPO</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{GRPO}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an unbiased estimator of <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi}(p)</annotation></semantics></math> (zero bias, high variance), <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{E}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{E}(p)</annotation></semantics></math> is a biased estimator (non-zero bias, low variance) due to pooling samples from different states. A good <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> estimator achieves a larger reduction in variance than the square of its introduced bias.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{SAE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>SAE</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{SAE}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> vs <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{GRPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>GRPO</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{GRPO}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem A.7 (SAE optimally reduces estimation-to-class error). ‣ A.7 SAE Improves Estimation of the Best Consistent Value Function ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Proofs ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a> guarantees that projecting GRPO estimates into <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> reduces the estimation-to-class distance in <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is an <span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">estimation</span> improvement relative to the feasible class <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, but it does not by itself imply <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\mathrm{SAE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>SAE</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\mathrm{SAE}}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly closer to the true <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> than <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>GRPO</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}</annotation></semantics></math> unless <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is well-approximated by <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{E}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> vs <math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{SAE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>SAE</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{SAE}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> There is no unconditional ordering: <math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> trades variance for (potential) bias, while <math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{SAE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>SAE</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{SAE}}</annotation></semantics></math> enforces structural consistency and reduces estimation-to-class error. Which estimator is closer to <math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on (i) how well <math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> matches <math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> and (ii) the bias magnitude of <math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> within each subtree.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.8 </span>On mean-centering without standardization.</h3>

<div id="A1.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A common practice in policy-gradient methods is to normalize advantages by both mean and standard deviation (z-scoring). However, in the staged setting this can distort reward magnitudes and interfere with the tree-structured consistency of prefix values. Our approach applies only mean-centering, which is both simpler and theoretically justified.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Claim A.8</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> be unbiased advantage estimates with variance <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Among all affine transformations <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}_{k}=(A_{k}-b)/c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}_{k}=(A_{k}-b)/c</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the choice <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\mathbb{E}[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\mathbb{E}[A]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=1</annotation></semantics></math> minimizes the variance of the stochastic policy-gradient estimator</p>
<table id="A1.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}=\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}A^{\prime}_{k}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a_{k}\mid s_{k})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}=\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}A^{\prime}_{k}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(a_{k}\mid s_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The variance of <math id="A1.SS8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}</annotation></semantics></math> is proportional to <math id="A1.SS8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[A^{\prime}]\cdot\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\|^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[A^{\prime}]\cdot\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\|^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. For affine transformations,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[A^{\prime}]=\operatorname{Var}[(A-b)/c]=\tfrac{1}{c^{2}}\operatorname{Var}[A]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[A^{\prime}]=\operatorname{Var}[(A-b)/c]=\tfrac{1}{c^{2}}\operatorname{Var}[A].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS8.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> only rescales variance without affecting direction of <math id="A1.SS8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimizer is <math id="A1.SS8.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=1</annotation></semantics></math>. The optimal <math id="A1.SS8.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> is the mean <math id="A1.SS8.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[A]</annotation></semantics></math>, which achieves the global minimum <math id="A1.SS8.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[A-b]=\operatorname{Var}[A]-\operatorname{Var}[A]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[A-b]=\operatorname{Var}[A]-\operatorname{Var}[A]=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, mean-centering (without standardization) uniquely minimizes gradient variance.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This explains why simple mean-centering suffices: it reduces gradient variance while avoiding the instability and bias introduced by scaling with an estimated standard deviation.<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            Standardization may reduce sensitivity to reward scale across unrelated tasks, but in tree-structured reasoning trajectories the scale itself is meaningful, making mean-centering the variance-optimal choice.</span></span></span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.9 </span>Monte–Carlo baseline: unbiasedness and variance</h3>

<div id="A1.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(1)},\dots,r^{(M)}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(1)},\dots,r^{(M)}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent outcomes of rollouts from prefix <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the empirical estimator</p>
<table id="A1.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{M}(p)=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}r^{(m)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{M}(p)=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}r^{(m)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Unbiasedness is immediate:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\widehat{V}_{M}(p)]=\mathbb{E}[r\mid p]=V(p)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\widehat{V}_{M}(p)]=\mathbb{E}[r\mid p]=V(p).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The variance satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}[\widehat{V}_{M}(p)]=\frac{\operatorname{Var}[r\mid p]}{M}=\frac{V(p)(1-V(p))}{M}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}[\widehat{V}_{M}(p)]=\frac{\operatorname{Var}[r\mid p]}{M}=\frac{V(p)(1-V(p))}{M},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.4" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Central Limit Theorem, for large <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{M}(p)\approx\mathcal{N}\!\big(V(p),\,V(p)(1-V(p))/M\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{M}(p)\approx\mathcal{N}\!\big(V(p),\,V(p)(1-V(p))/M\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.5" class="ltx_p">so a (Gaussian) approximate <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\!-\!\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\!-\!\delta</annotation></semantics></math> confidence interval has half-width <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{-1}(1-\delta/2)\sqrt{V(p)(1-V(p))/M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{-1}(1-\delta/2)\sqrt{V(p)(1-V(p))/M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
A conservative non-asymptotic bound follows from Hoeffding’s inequality:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\big(|\widehat{V}_{M}(p)-V(p)|\geq\epsilon\big)\leq 2\exp(-2M\epsilon^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\big(|\widehat{V}_{M}(p)-V(p)|\geq\epsilon\big)\leq 2\exp(-2M\epsilon^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.6" class="ltx_p">These identities quantify the compute–variance tradeoff: sparse rewards (small <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(p)</annotation></semantics></math>) require large <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> to reduce baseline noise, motivating the low-cost, biased heuristics we use in practice (Sec. <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Staged Advantage Estimation as Constrained Quadratic Program ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experimental Setup: Hyperparameters and Model Configuration</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section details the hyperparameter and model settings used for both Tree-OPO and GPRO training as well as the training setting combines the distillation-based methods.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Policy Optimization Objectives.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our policy <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is optimized using a combined objective, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{policy}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>policy</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{policy}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which integrates a GRPO-style policy gradient term, <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">optionally</span> with a distillation loss:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L_{\text{policy}}=-\mathbb{E}_{\tau}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\log\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}|s_{t})A^{\pi_{\theta}}(s_{t},a_{t})\right]+\beta_{\text{distill}}D_{\text{KL}}(\pi_{\text{teacher}}(a_{t}|s_{t})\|\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}|s_{t}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>policy</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>distill</mtext></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>teacher</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{policy}}=-\mathbb{E}_{\tau}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\log\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}|s_{t})A^{\pi_{\theta}}(s_{t},a_{t})\right]+\beta_{\text{distill}}D_{\text{KL}}(\pi_{\text{teacher}}(a_{t}|s_{t})\|\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}|s_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The first term represents the policy gradient loss (negative of the objective), where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\pi_{\theta}}(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\pi_{\theta}}(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is the advantage from Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Staged Advantage Estimation as Constrained Quadratic Program ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>. The <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> parameter (0.5) serves as the weighting coefficient for the baseline component within the advantage estimation (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime}_{i}=r_{i}-\alpha V(p_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime}_{i}=r_{i}-\alpha V(p_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>). The second term is an optional distillation loss. When distillation is applied, it is weighed by the <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">distillation coefficient </span> (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{distill}}=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>distill</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{distill}}=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>). Otherwise, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{distill}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>distill</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{distill}}</annotation></semantics></math> is set to <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. We utilize <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">reverse KL divergence</span>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(P\|Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(P\|Q)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is the distribution of teacher policies (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{teacher}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>teacher</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{teacher}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is the distribution of student policies (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>). This choice promotes student coverage of the teacher’s distributional modes, crucial for tasks with multiple valid reasoning paths. Separate learning rates are specified for the primary GRPO policy (<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">3e-5</span>) and for the distillation loss component (<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">5e-4</span>), or in specific distillation-only training regimes <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">when distillation is enabled</span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A2.T3.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A2.T3.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Parameter</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T3.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Value</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A2.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.T3.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> (Advantage Baseline Weight)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T3.3.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0.5</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Distillation Coefficient (<math id="A2.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{distill}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>distill</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{distill}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0.1</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Model Precision</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">bf16</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Teacher Precision</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">bf16</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Group Size</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Max Prompt Length</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.7.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">256 (GRPO), 512 (Tree-OPO)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.8.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Max Sequence Length</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.8.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">512 (GRPO), 768 (Tree-OPO)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.9.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Top-<math id="A2.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> (Sampling)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.9.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.10.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Top-<math id="A2.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> (Sampling)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.10.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1.0</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.11.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Temperature (Sampling)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.11.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1.0</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.12.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">KL Divergence Type</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.12.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Reverse</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.13.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Optimizer</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.13.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">AdamW</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.14" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.14.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Batch size</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.14.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">32</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.15" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.15.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Learning rate (Policy, GRPO)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.15.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.15.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3e-5</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.16" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.16.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.16.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Learning rate (Policy, Distillation)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.16.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.16.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5e-4</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.17" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.17.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.17.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">LR Scheduler</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.17.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.17.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Cosine</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.18" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.18.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.18.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Critic Head Architecture</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.18.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.18.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Llama Decoder</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.19" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.19.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.19.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Critic Warm-up Epochs</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.19.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.19.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.20" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.20.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.20.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Critic Algorithm</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.20.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.20.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Actor-Critic with TD(<math id="A2.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.21" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.21.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.21.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">GAE_gamma (<math id="A2.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.21.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.21.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0.95</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.22" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.22.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.22.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">PEFT LoRA Rank (r)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.22.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.22.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.23" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.23.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T3.3.23.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">PEFT LoRA Alpha (<math id="A2.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\text{LoRA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mtext>LoRA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\text{LoRA}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.23.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T3.3.23.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">64</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.3.24" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T3.3.24.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="A2.T3.3.24.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">PEFT LoRA Dropout</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.3.24.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A2.T3.3.24.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0.1</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T3.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A2.T3.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Hyperparameter and model settings for Tree-PRO, encompassing GRPO and distillation components.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Critic Model and Loss.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The critic network learns a state-value function, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\phi}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\phi}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, to estimate expected returns from prefixes. Its <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama Decoder</span> architecture allows it to process sequence contexts for value prediction <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GAE_gamma</span> (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.95</annotation></semantics></math>) is the discount factor for Generalized Advantage Estimation (GAE). The critic’s loss, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{critic}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>critic</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{critic}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is a Mean Squared Error (MSE) between its prediction and the computed target value:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{critic}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(V_{\phi}(s_{i})-V^{\text{target}}_{i})^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>critic</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{critic}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(V_{\phi}(s_{i})-V^{\text{target}}_{i})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\text{target}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\text{target}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Generalized Advantage Estimation (GAE) return for state <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Additional Model Settings.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All models, including student and teacher, utilize <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bf16</span> precision. Generation sampling employs <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Top-p</span> (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>) with <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Temperature</span> <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>. The <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Group Size</span> for GRPO batching is 8. Standard GRPO configurations use maximum prompt and sequence lengths of 256 and 512 tokens respectively, while Tree-OPO setups extend these to 512 and 768. Parameter Efficient Fine-Tuning (PEFT) via LoRA is applied, configured with a LoRA <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">rank</span> of 16, a scaling <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">alpha</span> of 64, and a <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dropout</span> rate of 0.1.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">QP Solver.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For our staged advantage estimation (SAE) solver, we employ both hard-constrained and soft-constrained quadratic programming (QP) formulations. Both versions use <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">scipy.optimize.minimize</span> with the <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SLSQP</span> method.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">hard-constrained</span> QP, a margin of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=1\times 10^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=1\times 10^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math> is enforced on triplet-consistency constraints, with the optimizer’s maximum iterations set to <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math> and function tolerance at <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-8}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">soft-constrained</span> version, which is more stable and computationally efficient, the optimization problem is defined as:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\bm{a}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}}\quad\|\bm{a}-\bm{r}\|^{2}+\lambda\sum_{(i,j)\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{order}}}\max(0,a_{i}-a_{j}+\delta)^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒓</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>order</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\bm{a}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}}\quad\|\bm{a}-\bm{r}\|^{2}+\lambda\sum_{(i,j)\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{order}}}\max(0,a_{i}-a_{j}+\delta)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We set the regularization strength <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> and the margin <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=1\times 10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=1\times 10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>. In all cases, the optimizer is initialized with a warm start using mean-centered rewards to ensure fast and stable convergence.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Staged Advantage Estimation: A Minimal Example</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To illustrate the structure of our staged prompting setup and the computation of advantages, we present a minimal example derived from the reasoning tree described in Figure <a href="#S3.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ Offline teacher-generated prefixes. ‣ 3.1 Problem Setting and MCTS-Derived Prefix Tree ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Each prompt chain represents an incremental sequence of reasoning steps towards a solution, beginning with a base question (Q) and extended by alphabet-labeled stages (e.g., A, B, C).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F5.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.09284v1/figure/staged_prompts.png" id="A3.F5.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:476/653;" width="476" height="653" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F5.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A3.F5.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">A group of staged prompts. </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F5.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.09284v1/figure/note_text_pairs.png" id="A3.F5.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/199;" width="476" height="199" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F5.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A3.F5.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Correspondence between reasoning nodes and textual content. Each node represents a reasoning step in a multi-hop prompt.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A3.F5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Illustration of Staged Reasoning Prompts and Text Mappings.<span id="A3.F5.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (a) A group of example staged prompts. Each row is a distinct prompt chain, and the checkmark/cross indicates whether the model produced a correct final answer when conditioned on that prompt. (b) Correspondence between symbolic reasoning nodes (Q, A, B, etc.) and their textual content. Each node represents a distinct reasoning step, forming compositional instructions separated by double newlines (<span id="A3.F5.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">\n\n</span>) in the actual prompt fed to the language model.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix C Staged Advantage Estimation: A Minimal Example ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> presents success statistics and heuristic value estimations (<math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{exp}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{exp}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{opt}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{opt}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{pes}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>pes</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{pes}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>). As detailed in Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Staged Advantage Estimation as Constrained Quadratic Program ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, advantage optimization is guided by <span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">tree consistency constraints</span> (<math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{order}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>order</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{order}}</annotation></semantics></math>), ensuring coherent advantage signals.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">expected value baseline</span> (<math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{exp}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{exp}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>), calculated as average success rate, inherently aligns with these constraints, yielding precise ’surprise’ signals. For instance, ‘<math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{pair}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>pair</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{pair}}</annotation></semantics></math>‘ requires <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}&lt;a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}&lt;a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for a failing parent <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> leading to a successful child <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Comparing ‘Q-A-B‘ (<math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E[R]=1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E[R]=1/3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>) and its successful descendant ‘Q-A-B-C‘ (<math id="A3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E[R]=1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E[R]=1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=1</annotation></semantics></math> from ‘t0‘), <math id="A3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math> generates advantages of <math id="A3.p3.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-1/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1/6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3/4</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, satisfying <math id="A3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}&lt;a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}&lt;a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. While this example doesn’t fully capture all ‘<math id="A3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{triplet}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>triplet</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{triplet}}</annotation></semantics></math>‘ conditions, <math id="A3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s accurate value estimations (<math id="A3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E[R|\text{Q-A-B}]=1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mtext>Q-A-B</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E[R|\text{Q-A-B}]=1/3</annotation></semantics></math> vs <math id="A3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E[R|\text{Q-E-F}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mtext>Q-E-F</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E[R|\text{Q-E-F}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>) are fundamental for enabling such fine-grained control over advantage ordering.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Conversely, <span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">optimistic</span> (<math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{opt}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{opt}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>) and <span id="A3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">pessimistic</span> (<math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{pes}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>pes</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{pes}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>) baselines often violate these constraints. <math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{pes}}(\text{Q-E-F})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>pes</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Q-E-F</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{pes}}(\text{Q-E-F})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{pes}}(\text{Q-A-B})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>pes</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Q-A-B</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{pes}}(\text{Q-A-B})=0</annotation></semantics></math> despite different <math id="A3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E[R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E[R]</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, <math id="A3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{opt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{opt}}</annotation></semantics></math> assigns 1 to ‘Q-A-B‘, ‘Q-A-B-C‘, and ‘Q-A-J‘ (all having different <math id="A3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E[R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E[R]</annotation></semantics></math>), losing vital discriminative power for tree consistency.</p>
</div>
