<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Example staged advantage values computed as <math id="A3.T5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R-\alpha V(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R-\alpha V(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for different heuristic baselines. The <span id="A3.T5.20" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">expectation baseline</span> (<math id="A3.T5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math>; second column, shaded) better satisfies the <em id="A3.T5.21" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">tree-consistency constraints</em>, reflecting coherent advantage values aligned with reward structure across the tree. In contrast, the <span id="A3.T5.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">optimistic</span> (<math id="A3.T5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{opt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{opt}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <span id="A3.T5.23" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">pessimistic</span> (<math id="A3.T5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{pes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>pes</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{pes}}</annotation></semantics></math>) baselines exhibit more inconsistent or overly conservative adjustments. Each row corresponds to a prompt-completion trajectory with binary reward <math id="A3.T5.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> from Figure <a href="#A3.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix C Staged Advantage Estimation: A Minimal Example ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>(a).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Multi-Turn MCTS Rollout Structure and Tree Visualization</h2>

<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multi-turn Rollout.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following rStar <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qi+24</a>]</cite>, a reasoning episode is decomposed into stages <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math>, where at each stage the agent generates an action <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on a state <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and transitions to the next state via <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t+1}=s_{t}\circ a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t+1}=s_{t}\circ a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. This defines a multi-turn rollout, where the final solution is constructed as a chain of reasoning steps <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{1},\dots,a_{T}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{1},\dots,a_{T}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Unlike standard single-step MCTS, which performs search from a fixed root to a terminal state, rStar applies MCTS recursively over multiple stages, building up partial completions and branching decisions at each intermediate node. The result is a structured, non-Markovian tree of reasoning trajectories, where each visited prefix <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a meaningful subproblem along a candidate path. Thus, the training data is not drawn directly from an offline teacher policy, but rather sampled from a <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">complex, multi-turn distribution</em> induced by search—reflecting the teacher’s internal planning dynamics across many possible intermediate reasoning paths. Figure <a href="#A4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Learning from the MCTS-Induced Distribution. ‣ Appendix D Multi-Turn MCTS Rollout Structure and Tree Visualization ‣ Tree-OPO: Off-policy Monte Carlo Tree-Guided Advantage Optimization for Multistep Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> iillustrates a reasoning tree produced by the multi-turn MCTS rollout process.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Learning from the MCTS-Induced Distribution.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although the MCTS-derived distribution over prefixes does not correspond to samples from a stationary expert policy, it is shaped by a structured search process guided by value estimates and exploration. Each prefix <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> encountered during multi-turn rollout reflects a plausible intermediate reasoning state prioritized during search. From an RL perspective, this yields an offline dataset composed of staged pairs <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{t},c_{t},R_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{t},c_{t},R_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, where completions <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and rewards <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are conditioned on prefix context. This structured distribution captures diverse yet high-quality trajectories that extend beyond single-path demonstrations. By leveraging this data with policy gradient methods and advantage estimation, the student can effectively optimize its policy without requiring direct imitation. Thus, the learning process exploits the inductive bias of the MCTS-induced distribution to supervise training in a way that aligns with structured reasoning dynamics.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.F6" class="ltx_figure ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:155.5pt;height:550pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><div class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="width:550.0pt;transform:translate(-197.3pt,-197.3pt) rotate(-90deg) ;"><figure><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.09284v1/concert_ticket_reasoning_tree.svg" id="A4.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:759/196;" width="759" height="196"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="A4.F6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center" style="font-size:90%;">A visualization of a multi-turn MCTS tree to a question in GSM8k.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Algorithm</h2>

<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm">
<div id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.3.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Teacher MCTS budget <math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B,d_{\max},b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B,d_{\max},b)</annotation></semantics></math>; student policy <math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>; batch size <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>; baseline rollouts <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>; scaling <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>; solver option; learning rate <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Updated parameters <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Offline MCTS:</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.3.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm1.3.4.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">training problem</em> <span id="algorithm1.3.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Run multi-turn MCTS (<math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> rollouts, depth <math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq d_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq d_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, branching <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq b</annotation></semantics></math>)
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Collect trajectories and augment with all prefixes <math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> prefix tree <math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.7" class="ltx_listingline">end foreach
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.3.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <em id="algorithm1.3.8.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not converged</em> <span id="algorithm1.3.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Sample <math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> prefixes <math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{k}\}\subset\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{k}\}\subset\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.3.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm1.3.10.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\dots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\dots,K</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.3.10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Rollout <math id="algorithm1.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{c}_{k}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid p_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}_{k}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid p_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>; reward <math id="algorithm1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> end for
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Estimate baseline <math id="algorithm1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(p_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(p_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> (<em id="algorithm1.3.13.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">MC</em>, empirical, optimistic/pessimistic)
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Compute <math id="algorithm1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime}_{k}\leftarrow r_{k}-\alpha V(p_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime}_{k}\leftarrow r_{k}-\alpha V(p_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>; mean-center <math id="algorithm1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}\to\{a_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}\to\{a_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.3.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm1.3.15.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">SAE enabled</em> <span id="algorithm1.3.15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.16" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Refine <math id="algorithm1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> via heuristic or constrained QP
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.17" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> end if
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.18" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}\leftarrow\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{k}a_{k}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\hat{c}_{k}\mid p_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}\leftarrow\tfrac{1}{K}\sum_{k}a_{k}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\hat{c}_{k}\mid p_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.19" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Update <math id="algorithm1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\theta+\eta\,\widehat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\theta+\eta\,\widehat{g}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.20" class="ltx_listingline">end while
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.21" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Tree-OPO: Tree-structured Relative Policy Optimization</figcaption>
</figure>
